## 🔬 Component-Level Analysis

### Time Distribution by Component Type

| Case | LLM (s) | LLM % | MCP/Tools (s) | MCP % | Init (s) | Init % | Other (s) | Other % |
|------|---------|-------|---------------|-------|----------|--------|-----------|---------|
| **Case 1** | 4.85 | 99.8% | 0.01 | 0.2% | 0 | 0% | 0 | 0% |
| **Case 3** | 16.72 | 55.9% | 4.12 | 13.8% | 1.09 | 3.6% | 7.98 | 26.7% |
| **Case 4** | 14.0 | 62.7% | 1.5 | 6.7% | 0.54 | 2.4% | 6.28 | 28.1% |
| **Case 5 P1** | 30.0 | 82.3% | 3.0 | 8.2% | 4.0 | 11.0% | 2.45 | 6.7% |
| **Case 5 P2** | 36.0 | 80.4% | 3.0 | 6.7% | 2.0 | 4.5% | 3.8 | 8.5% |

### Key Observations

1. **LLM Dominance is Universal**
   - Minimum: 55.9% (Case 3 - balanced workflow)
   - Maximum: 99.8% (Case 1 - pure routing)
   - Average: 76.2% across all cases

2. **MCP/Tool Execution is Fast**
   - Average: 2.72s per case
   - Usually 5-15% of total time
   - Well-optimized API calls

3. **Initialization Overhead**
   - SSE connection: 1-4s
   - Negligible for long-running operations
   - Could be pooled/reused for optimization

