## ⚡ Parallel vs Sequential Comparison

### Case 5 Phase 2: Impact of Parallelization

```mermaid
---
config:
    xyChart:
        width: 900
        height: 600
    themeVariables:
        xyChart:
            titleColor: "#2c3e50"
            plotColorPalette: "#e74c3c,#2ecc71"
---
xychart-beta
    title "Sequential vs Parallel Execution - Case 5 Tasks"
    x-axis ["Sequential", "Parallel (Actual)"]
    y-axis "Total Task Time (seconds)" 0 --> 80
    bar [75.7, 30.5]
```

**Performance Gain Details**:

| Metric | Sequential | Parallel | Improvement |
|--------|-----------|----------|-------------|
| **Task 1** (Set AC) | 21.5s | 21.5s | Same |
| **Task 2** (Light on) | 30.5s | 30.5s | Same |
| **Task 3** (Light off) | 23.7s | 23.7s | Same |
| **Total Time** | **75.7s** | **30.5s** | **-59.8%** ⚡ |
| **Time Saved** | - | **45.2s** | **60% faster** |

**Why it works**:
- Each task is independent
- No shared resources (separate MCP sessions)
- ThreadPoolExecutor efficiently manages 3 concurrent Tool Agents
- Bottleneck becomes the slowest task (Task 2: 30.5s)

